{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01459",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.24,
      "end_seconds": 7.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Okay, um, so hi, doctor, I hope I'm not disturbing you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.06,
      "end_seconds": 13.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "Come in. Please sit. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.88,
      "end_seconds": 17.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "I've been feeling faint."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.34,
      "end_seconds": 21.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "How long has it been like this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.47,
      "end_seconds": 36.62,
      "duration_seconds": 14.15,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, uh, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 38.54,
      "end_seconds": 47.28,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.0,
      "end_seconds": 82.63,
      "duration_seconds": 33.63,
      "text": "Ah, only lying down, and it's not much. It feels moderate to me. Yes, standing. That makes it worse. It's on and off. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. Let me think, um, and there's stomach pain as well, three weeks now. About stomach pain, I'd say severe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.87,
      "end_seconds": 87.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.31,
      "end_seconds": 94.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Yes, I had a caesarean for my second baby, nine years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.77,
      "end_seconds": 99.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 100.54,
      "end_seconds": 112.58,
      "duration_seconds": 12.04,
      "text": "I have high cholesterol, for about a year. Yes, gout. I have arthritis in my knees, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.16,
      "end_seconds": 116.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Right, and anything else to add?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.26,
      "end_seconds": 121.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.58,
      "text": "Yes, gout is known to us, good to have that clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 130.45,
      "end_seconds": 135.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.04,
      "end_seconds": 140.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "No, not that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.82,
      "end_seconds": 154.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 156.38,
      "end_seconds": 160.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.18,
      "text": "Yeah, um, I take simvastatin, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.54,
      "end_seconds": 165.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "Alright, do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.25,
      "end_seconds": 177.23,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "20 milligrams, I think that's what's on the box. Allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day for the gout."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.64,
      "end_seconds": 178.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Hm, okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 179.75,
      "end_seconds": 183.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Paracetamol. I take it 650 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 184.52,
      "end_seconds": 186.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.38,
      "end_seconds": 191.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "I'll have a glass of wine with dinner."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.28,
      "end_seconds": 193.46,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.4,
      "end_seconds": 198.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "I smoke roughly a pack every two days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.28,
      "end_seconds": 201.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.38,
      "end_seconds": 208.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.05,
      "end_seconds": 212.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.22,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.87,
      "end_seconds": 218.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.73,
      "end_seconds": 220.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.3,
      "end_seconds": 227.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.57,
      "end_seconds": 231.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "Any fever or chest pain at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 233.2,
      "end_seconds": 235.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "None of those, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.74,
      "end_seconds": 240.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Mm-hmm. On the cardiac side, anything I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.24,
      "end_seconds": 244.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Mm, no, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.21,
      "end_seconds": 250.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Okay, I'll note down your vital signs first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 256.39,
      "end_seconds": 258.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.52,
      "end_seconds": 278.14,
      "duration_seconds": 8.62,
      "text": "Okay: blood pressure 133 over 70, heart rate 114, SpO2 97 percent on room air, respiratory rate 17."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.84,
      "end_seconds": 282.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.6,
      "end_seconds": 285.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.1,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.68,
      "end_seconds": 288.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.04,
      "end_seconds": 308.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "You look pale, your pulse is fast and your tummy is tender at the top."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.11,
      "end_seconds": 316.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Alright, thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.23,
      "end_seconds": 340.07,
      "duration_seconds": 7.84,
      "text": "So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with a possible bleeding stomach ulcer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.93,
      "end_seconds": 344.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.11,
      "end_seconds": 372.88,
      "duration_seconds": 26.77,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a possible bleeding stomach ulcer, and we'll know more once the an endoscopy is back. Let's book an endoscopy to look into bleeding. Please stop the ibuprofen and do not eat or drink. Come back or go to emergency straight away if you vomit again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 373.44,
      "end_seconds": 375.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.81,
      "end_seconds": 381.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I'd like you back straight away. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 382.05,
      "end_seconds": 383.88,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    }
  ]
}